So it is best to regroup the accident causes so that a good analysis can be done. The groupings will be decided as such :

- speeding since it as the greatest numbers of 15296 amongst all other groups and has to be a standalone.

- Reckless Driving: Known to be deliberate and unsafe manoeuvres on the road, which will be an interesting cause to be studies within the urbans areas.

- Driver state/Fatigue : Known to be driver-state issues, which is a psychological type of group that is separate from the deliberate risk-takers and is hence worth studying on its own.

- Vehicle Failure : Mechnical issues, it is also worth knowing to see if imposes on vehicle maintenance or scrapping is required.

- Alcohol/Drugs : it is an important standalone cause that is enforceable and well-studied, it is also difficult to lump this category therefore under others or any other groups

- Environmental: Accidents can occur due to mother nature which may an influence worth noting in Thailand

- Others


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
acc <- acc %>%
  mutate(
    cause_grp = case_when(

      # Speeding 
      str_detect(presumed_cause,
                 regex("^speeding$", ignore_case = TRUE)) ~ "Speeding",

      # Alcohol/Drugs
      str_detect(presumed_cause,
                 regex("alcohol|psychoactive|มึนเมา",
                       ignore_case = TRUE)) ~ "Alcohol / Drugs",

      # Fatigue
      str_detect(presumed_cause,
                 regex("falling asleep|fatigue|drowsy|medical condition|mobile phone",
                       ignore_case = TRUE)) ~ "Fatigue",

      # Reckless Driving
      str_detect(presumed_cause,
                 regex("cutting in|illegal overtaking|aggressive|loss of control|tailgat|abrupt lane|sudden stop|straddling|reversing|running red light|ignore.*stop|failure to yield|wrong lane|without headlights|failure to signal|unfamiliar",
                       ignore_case = TRUE)) ~ "Reckless Driving",

      # Vehicle Failure
      str_detect(presumed_cause,
                 regex("equipment failure|tire|tyre|brake|electrical|turn signal|overloaded|disabled vehicle",
                       ignore_case = TRUE)) ~ "Vehicle Failure",

      # Environmental 
      str_detect(presumed_cause,
                 regex("debris|slippery|dangerous curve|insufficient light|visibility|road.*condition|construction|narrow|divider|traffic light|traffic sign|obstruction|repair|external disturbance|internal disturbance|no presumed cause",
                       ignore_case = TRUE)) ~ "Environmental",

      # Others 
      TRUE ~ "Others"
    ),

    cause_grp = factor(cause_grp, levels = c(
      "Speeding", "Reckless Driving", "Fatigue",
      "Vehicle Failure", "Alcohol / Drugs", "Environmental", "Others"
    ))
  )

# To verify the classification in case of errors
acc %>%
  st_drop_geometry() %>%
  count(cause_grp, sort = TRUE) %>%
  mutate(pct = round(100 * n / sum(n), 1))
```

